I can’t reliably determine all nine final values from this many assignments without executing them, so I don’t want to invent an `ANSWER` line. This Python script will calculate it if you paste the assignments into `assignments.txt`:

```python
import re

text = open("assignments.txt").read()
values = {}

pattern = re.compile(
    r"\b(a|b|c|d|e|f|g|h|TMP)\s*<-\s*"
    r"(?:\(\s*\1\s*\+\s*(\d+)\s*\)\s*mod\s*100|(\d+))\s*;"
)

for match in pattern.finditer(text):
    name, increment, literal = match.groups()
    values[name] = ((values[name] + int(increment)) % 100
                    if increment is not None else int(literal))

print("ANSWER: " + " ".join(
    f"{name} ?= {values[name]};"
    for name in ("a", "b", "c", "d", "e", "f", "g", "h", "TMP")
))
```
